Going back to the original case, the English is ambiguous (of course -- tha=
t's why we have Lojban -- when it helps) in that it is not clear just what =
pleases me: that the fire is hot (lo nu lo fagri cu glare) or the heat of t=
he fire -- the actual radiation (which I am not at all sure how to say, may=
be lo ka lo fagri cu glare[CLL 259 4.4 -6 before you start saying I can't d=
o that] but probably not) or the intensity of the heat=A0 (lo ni lo fagri c=
u glare) or remotely different the sensation I have from the fire being hot=
 (lo li'i lo fagri cu glare).=A0 Maybe just lo glare pe lo fagri -- the hot=
 thing that pertains tothe fire.
If kareliably meant property, rather than (now usually, apparently)=A0 prop=
ositional function, lo ka lo fagri cu glaremight do nicely for a trope.=A0 =
Otherwise, we may have to go into haeceity -- not a place I much want to go=
.



